 "discussion": "SYNOPSIS\n\nA mix of sun and cloud is expected today, with mainly cloudy conditions on Tuesday, as moisture at high levels pushes into the interior from a series of low-pressure systems tracking inland from the coast. Either day could feature a flurry or two. Winds will be generally light easterly today and will increase on Tuesday.\n\nEXTENDED OUTLOOK\n\nWednesday to Friday: Mainly cloudy conditions continue Wednesday and Thursday as a series of disturbances are ejected into the interior from a succession of coastal storms, carried by an increasing southwesterly flow aloft. Periods of light snow with minor accumulations are possible each day. A break in precipitation with partly cloudy skies is expected on Friday as a weak ridge builds over the southern interior. Maximum temperatures in the Alpine will be near minus 3°C on Wednesday and Thursday as the flow gradually warms, with highs again reaching near minus 3°C on Friday. Village highs will be near minus 1°C on Wednesday before rising to near zero on Thursday and Friday. Winds will continue to blow from the southeast 25 to 30 km/h on Wednesday, then shift to the southwest on Thursday at 25 to 35 km/h before diminishing to southwest 15 to 20 km/h on Friday.",
